 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation: gioja, Fiordiligi's “cresce, cresce” (Dorabella sings “cresce” once), and the toasts “Tocca e bevi” (the officers) and “Bevi e tocca” (the sisters) as many times as the score sets them. The chorus (bars 1–20 and 59–82, “Benedetti i doppi conjugi”) sings in the score and is heard with the piano, but has no role and no lines here. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L65, IPA checked against Castel), repeated where the score repeats the text; repeated fragments have short literal translations. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
